<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said it added some liquidity to the money market in the week to November 18 in order to offset a fall in bank note circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the  weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   414.27 (+  0.48)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  13.05 (-  0.30)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  3.23 (unchanged)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.81 (+  0.99)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 106.89 (-  0.80)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   449.01 (-  1.26)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
